%U A398944 1,4,2,1,2,2,1,4,5,1,8,3,7,2,8,5,0,4,0,8,8,9
%N A398944 Decimal expansion of the small face angle, in radians, of a canonical (dual-uniform) 10-gonal trapezohedron.
%C A398944 The 10-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 10-gonal antiprism.
%C A398944 Its faces are kites with one acute angle (this constant) and three obtuse angles (A398945).
%H A398944 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398944/b398944.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A398944 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Decagonal_antitegum">Decagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398944 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%F A398944 Equals arccos(2 - 3*(cos(Pi/10) - cos(Pi/5)) - cos(3*Pi/10)) = arccos(2 - 3*(A019881 - A019863) - A019845).
%F A398944 Equals arccos(c), where c = 0.986096... is the second smallest root of 16*x^4 - 176*x^3 + 436*x^2 - 336*x + 61.
%e A398944 0.16695003688682843038496946648938534286397893002557...
%t A398944 First[RealDigits[ArcCos[2 - 3*(Cos[Pi/10] - Cos[Pi/5]) - Cos[3*Pi/10]], 10, 100]]
%Y A398944 Cf. A398938 (volume), A398939 (surface area), A398940 (inradius), A398941 (midradius), A398942 (height).
%Y A398944 Cf. A398943 (long edge).
%Y A398944 Cf. A398945 (large face angle), A398946 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398944 Cf. A019845, A019863, A019881.
